From 269edcddccde7a22718b404e7b9956b1d0ed59da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kaiyue Wen <kaiyue@sc.stanford.edu>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 12:31:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add MuonH (Muon + hyperball constraint) record at K=3300
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MuonH (https://psychedelic-sunstone-851.notion.site/Fantastic-Pretraining-Optimizers-and-Where-to-Find-Them-2-1-Hyperball-Optimization-2e924306e6f280e7a5ffee00eb40a0dd)
replaces Muon's parameter-add update with a hyperball-projected variant
that preserves the Frobenius norm of every hidden 2D weight matrix throughout
training (hyperball_eps=1e-10). The orthogonalized direction is the same
12-iteration Newton-Schulz used by Muon; only the application step changes.

Per-module weight init std on top of the Frobenius-preserving update
(PyTorch default Kaiming uniform std listed in parens for reference):

- attn.proj std = 0.026  (default 0.0208, scaled ×1.25)
- mlp.proj  std = 0.031  (default 0.0104, scaled ×3.0)
- mlp.fc    std = 0.031  (default 0.0208, scaled ×1.5)
- qkv: PyTorch default

Hyperparameters: lr=0.018, h_cooldown_frac=1.0, aux_cooldown_frac=0.4,
muon_momentum=0.95.

Reliability: 5/5 capture-full hits across independent seeds at K=3300.
Final val_losses 3.27843 / 3.27950 / 3.27958 / 3.27981 / 3.27982 — all
below the 3.28 target. 200 steps below the current Muon SOTA at K=3500
on this benchmark.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
