From b6c036e91a8a920a7a903477cfb8c7a9d3cb5d9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kaiyue Wen <kaiyue@sc.stanford.edu>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 16:27:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Replace K=3300 record logfiles with hardened-script
 reruns
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the 5 K=3300 logfiles previously inlined from train_gpt_h.py
(which carried sweep machinery and a Muon fallback for zero-init hidden
matrices) with 5 fresh capture-full reruns whose embedded code is the
hardened, hyperparameter-hardcoded `train_gpt_simple_muonh.py` — i.e.
the script that, dropped in for `train_gpt_simple.py`, reproduces the
result via the standard quickstart command.

5 independent seeds: 4/5 hit val_loss <= 3.28 at K=3300; mean of all
5 = 3.27897, std = 0.00100. Seed 4 missed by 0.00016 (within seed
variance). Primary submitted logfile is seed 2 (3d5c5234), which hit
target one eval early at step 3250 (val_loss=3.27760).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
