From fad27b7c56b4d4510bcef9eceae1ce421d62212e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kaiyue Wen <kaiyue@sc.stanford.edu>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 10:46:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] track-3: bump MuonH record to K=3325 (10/10 hit, mean
 3.27821)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the 5-seed K=3300 record (4/5 hit, one seed missed by 0.00016)
with a 10-seed K=3325 result that is rock-solid: 10/10 hit, mean
val_loss=3.27821, std=0.00124. Same hardened script, same hyperparams
(matrix_lr=0.018, h_cooldown_frac=1.0, aux_cooldown_frac=0.4, per-module
init multipliers attn.proj×1.25, mlp.proj×3.0, mlp.fc×1.5). Primary
submitted logfile (results/9319c798-...txt) is seed 3 — the first to hit
the 3.28 target one eval early at step 3250 (val_loss=3.27528).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
